# Flow 7, a conflict on disk: the note changes on disk (another device's sync) while it is edited; the autosave finds it
# and asks "Changed on disk: Keep mine / Keep theirs"; the version not kept is written beside the note as
# "<name> (deck 2026-10-24 1403).md". Then the same on leaving (Esc).
seed note "Field log.md" field.md
seed setting open_in editor
wait 900
key ctrl-p
type field log
key enter
wait 500
expect state page editor
key ctrl-end
type Added on the deck.
disk write "Field log.md" theirs.md
wait 1800
expect state popup confirm
expect state popup_title "Changed on disk"
expect state last_save conflict
shot 01-conflict
check conflict
tap "Keep mine"
wait 400
expect state last_save kept-mine
expect state dirty 0
expect file "Field log.md" contains "First line.\nAdded on the deck."
expect copy "Field log.md" contains "Written on the laptop meanwhile."
shot 02-kept-mine
# Keep theirs: the note is read again, ours goes beside it
key ctrl-end
type  Second edit.
disk text "Field log.md" "# Field log\n\nThe laptop again.\n"
wait 1800
expect state popup confirm
tap "Keep theirs"
wait 400
expect state last_save kept-theirs
expect file "Field log.md" contains "The laptop again."
expect file "Field log.md" lacks "Second edit."
expect copy "Field log.md" contains "Added on the deck. Second edit."
shot 03-kept-theirs
# on leaving: Esc saves, finds the change, asks; the answer then goes back
key ctrl-end
type Third edit.
disk text "Field log.md" "# Field log\n\nA third device.\n"
key esc
wait 400
expect state popup confirm
expect state page editor
tap "Keep mine"
wait 500
expect state page home
expect file "Field log.md" contains "Third edit."
expect copy "Field log.md" contains "A third device."
